<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>ARE Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Apps and Tools Creation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In ARE, it is straightforward to declare <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">App</span> instances with tools. Any method of an <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">App</span> class can be transformed into a tool by adding simple decorators: <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@app_tool</span> to make it visible to the agent, <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@user_tool</span> to make it visible to the user only, and <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@env_tool</span> for external environment events.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@event_registered</span> decorator records tool calls in the <span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">EventLog</span>; each decorator must declare its <span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">OperationType</span> as <span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">read</span> or <span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">write</span> for the ARE Verifier to operate correctly.</p>
</div>
<figure id="LST1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<div id="LST1.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_Python ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
